# 32. Important Security Best Practices

1. Never make `/etc/shadow` world-readable.

2. Avoid manually editing `/etc/shadow`.

3. Use `passwd`, `chage`, and account-management tools.

4. Use strong passwords.

5. Restrict unnecessary administrative access.

6. Regularly review user accounts.

7. Disable or remove unused accounts according to your organization's policy.

8. Protect password hashes because stolen hashes can be attacked offline.

9. Never test password-cracking techniques against systems without authorization.

